# samba
# on server

- creating user, group, exports

sudo groupadd bigbang
sudo useradd -s /sbin/nologin -G bigbang penny
sudo mkdir -m 2770 -p /exports/bigbang
sudo chgrp bigbang /exports/bigbang
sudo semanage fcontext -a -t samba_share_t '/exports/bigbang(/.*)?'
sudo restorecon -RFv /exports/bigbang

- install samba samba-client
- in **/etc/samba/smb.conf** append:

[bigbang]
  path = /exports/bigbang
  valid users = @bigbang
  write list = @bigbang

- add samba user:
sudo smbpasswd -a penny

- start smb.service, enable samba in firewall
- **testparm** -- tests samba config parameters, see also <https://access.redhat.com/documentation/en-us/red_hat_enterprise_linux/7/html/system_administrators_guide/ch-file_and_print_servers#sect-Samba>

# on client:
- install cifs-utils
- create mountpoint
- create file with user credentials, e.g. /root/smb-multiuser.txt:
username=frank
password=pwd
- in /etc/fstab:
//serverX/smbspace /mnt/salesshare cifs credentials=/root/smb-multiuser.txt,multiuser,sec=ntlmssp 0 0

- or temporary mount:
mount -o username=rob //serverX/smbshare /mnt/rob


